  "caption": "Quinn chased a deeper squat with new flat shoes and extra sets. Next morning: a sore spot just above the kneecap.\n\nPain there may come from the quadriceps tendon, which gets loaded a lot in deep knee bends. It often follows a sudden jump in training, like more depth or volume.\n\nWhat often helps: adjust rather than stop, since complete rest can leave tendons less ready for load; try steady holds, which may ease pain for some; build slow, progressive strength; and use the next-day response as your guide. Tendons usually need months, so consistency matters.\n\nA sudden pop, or being unable to straighten the knee, needs same-day assessment, as does a hot, swollen or locked knee.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
